    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is this different from the fish oil I already take?",
            "answer": "<p>Most fish oil blends EPA and DHA together, often 180mg EPA and 120mg DHA in a<br/>standard capsule. AIWO EPA 500mg is standalone high-dose EPA. EPA is the<br/>anti-inflammatory omega-3, the fatty acid most linked to cardiovascular support<br/>and triglyceride balance. DHA has its own separate benefits for brain and retina.<br/>This is for people who want targeted EPA, not a general blend.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is Vitamin E in the formula?",
            "answer": "<p>EPA is a polyunsaturated fatty acid, so it is prone to oxidation. When fish oil<br/>oxidizes inside a capsule it degrades before it reaches your cells, and it causes<br/>the fishy aftertaste and reflux many people get. Vitamin E at 10mg, 100% of your<br/>daily RDA, is here to protect the EPA from oxidizing inside the capsule. It is an<br/>antioxidant stabilizer, not a cosmetic add-on.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can anyone add this to their routine?",
            "answer": "<p>It is designed for general adult use. If you are pregnant, breastfeeding, on blood<br/>thinners, or on cardiac or other ongoing medication, consult your doctor before<br/>starting.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I take it day to day?",
            "answer": "<p>Take 1 capsule with your main meal, swallowed whole. Increase to 2 only if your practitioner recommends it. The benefit comes from consistency, so build it into a fixed daily moment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WyBt4K": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I notice a difference?",
            "answer": "<p>EPA integrates into red blood cell membranes over 30 to 60 days, shifting your Omega-3 Index. Clinical studies on EPA and triglyceride support have used 8 to 12week intervention periods. Skipping doses interrupts that process. Track your lipid panel and Omega-3 Index at baseline and 90 days with AIWO 181 blood markers.<br/>Individual results vary.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
